Chapter: FsHandlerInstall

  cites Foreword chapter FileSystem

Section: Entry

 The arm for the default FileSystem handler INSTALL, and it deliberately
 does not assert what the read answers. No block device is attached, so
 the servicer reaches `fat16` and finds no volume; what is under test is
 that the slot holds the servicer's real address and control comes back.

 On the RISC-V emitter before the scratch-register fix, the slot received
 the low half of an address, the jump landed nowhere, and `after` never
 printed.

  opening : [Console, FileSystem.Read "NOPE"] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni "before"
    missing <- read-text "NOPE.TXT"
    print-line-uni ("len " & show (text-length missing))
    print-line-uni "after"
  end
